A: so Devops can scale consumers pods ?


Yes—DevOps can scale consumer Pods. If each Pod runs one consumer with the same group.id, Kafka redistributes the partitions among them.
For your 3-partition topic:
- 1 Pod → one consumer reads all 3 partitions.
- 2 Pods → consumers get 2 partitions and 1 partition.
- 3 Pods → each consumer gets 1 partition.
- 4 Pods → one consumer has no partition and stays idle.
In Kubernetes, DevOps changes the Deployment’s replica count, usually through Helm/GitOps, or configures autoscaling.
Adding Pods won’t always improve throughput: partition count limits parallelism, and a slow shared database can remain the bottleneck.
